e":35},[32,946,947],{"class":53},"#[cfg(feature ",[32,949,160],{"class":45},[32,951,952],{"class":66}," \"json\"",[32,954,955],{"class":53},")]\n",[32,957,958,961,964],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,959,960],{"class":45},"mod",[32,962,963],{"class":49}," json",[32,965,166],{"class":53},[14,967,969],{"id":968},"cargolock",[29,970,971],{},"Cargo.lock",[478,973,974,977,988],{},[481,975,976],{},"Pin exact versions resolved for your dependency graph.",[481,978,979,980,983,984,987],{},"Always commit for ",[139,981,982],{},"binaries",". For ",[139,985,986],{},"libraries"," the official recommendation is also to commit it, but it's commonly gitignored.",[481,989,990,993,994,997],{},[29,991,992],{},"cargo update"," bumps within semver-compatible range; ",[29,995,996],{},"cargo update -p serde --precise 1.0.150"," pins a single crate.",[14,999,1001],{"id":1000},"workspaces","Workspaces",[78,1003,1004,1005,1008],{},"When multiple crates share a workspace, dependency versions unify and ",[29,1006,1007],{},"target\u002F"," is shared:",[19,1010,1011],{"language":644},[23,1012,1014],{"className":647,"code":1013,"language":644,"meta":27,"style":27},"# Cargo.toml (workspace root)\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"crates\u002F*\", \"app\"]\n\n[workspace.dependencies]\nserde = \"1.0\"\n",[29,1015,1016,1021,1026,1031,1035,1040],{"__ignoreMap":27},[32,1017,1018],{"class":34,"line":35},[32,1019,1020],{},"# Cargo.toml (workspace root)\n",[32,1022,1023],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,1024,1025],{},"[workspace]\n",[32,1027,1028],{"class":34,"line":57},[32,1029,1030],{},"members = [\"crates\u002F*\", \"app\"]\n",[32,1032,1033],{"class":34,"line":73},[32,1034,701],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":700},[32,1036,1037],{"class":34,"line":214},[32,1038,1039],{},"[workspace.dependencies]\n",[32,1041,1042],{"class":34,"line":239},[32,1043,872],{},[78,1045,1046,1047,1050],{},"Members then reference with ",[29,1048,1049],{},"serde.workspace = true",".",[14,1052,1054],{"id":1053},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[478,1056,1057,1066,1086,1102,1122,1135],{},[481,1058,1059,1061,1062,1065],{},[139,1060,413],{},": ",[29,1063,1064],{},"rustc --explain E0382"," (or any error code from a compiler message) prints a detailed explanation with examples, straight from the compiler — faster than searching online for a common error code.",[481,1067,1068,1071,1072,1075,1076,1079,1080,1082,1083,1085],{},[139,1069,1070],{},"Idiom",": use ",[29,1073,1074],{},"println!(\"{name:?}\")"," (Debug) while prototyping and switch to ",[29,1077,1078],{},"println!(\"{name}\")"," (Display) once a type has a hand-written ",[29,1081,405],{}," impl — reaching for ",[29,1084,409],{}," everywhere works but produces developer-facing, not user-facing, output.",[481,1087,1088,1090,1091,1094,1095,1097,1098,1101],{},[139,1089,1070],{},": set ",[29,1092,1093],{},"publish = false"," in ",[29,1096,640],{}," immediately for any project that isn't meant for crates.io — it costs nothing and prevents an accidental ",[29,1099,1100],{},"cargo publish"," months later when you've forgotten the project was never meant to be public.",[481,1103,1104,1061,1106,1109,1110,1113,1114,1118,1119,1121],{},[139,1105,413],{},[29,1107,1108],{},"cargo run -- --flag value"," — everything after the bare ",[29,1111,1112],{},"--"," is passed to ",[1115,1116,1117],"em",{},"your"," binary's argv, not interpreted by Cargo; forgetting the ",[29,1120,1112],{}," is a common reason \"my CLI flag doesn't work\" during local testing.",[481,1123,1124,1126,1127,1130,1131,1134],{},[139,1125,1070],{},": pin dependencies with ",[29,1128,1129],{},"\"=\""," only when you have a specific reason (a known-broken later version, reproducibility requirements) — the default caret (",[29,1132,1133],{},"^",") requirement is usually right, since it allows patch\u002Fminor updates that are supposed to be backward compatible under semver.",[481,1136,1137,1061,1140,1143,1144,1146,1147,1150,1151,296,1154,296,1157,1160],{},[139,1138,1139],{},"Performance",[29,1141,1142],{},"cargo new","'s default ",[29,1145,640],{}," doesn't set a release profile — for anything beyond a quick script, add ",[29,1148,1149],{},"[profile.release]"," tuning (",[29,1152,1153],{},"lto",[29,1155,1156],{},"codegen-units",[29,1158,1159],{},"strip",") once you're past the prototyping stage, since the untouched defaults favor compile speed over runtime performance.",[14,1162,1164],{"id":1163},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[478,1166,1167,1187,1204,1222,1236,1245],{},[481,1168,1169,1175,1176,1179,1180,1183,1184,1050],{},[139,1170,1171,1172],{},"Binaries from ",[29,1173,1174],{},"src\u002Fbin\u002F*.rs",": each ",[29,1177,1178],{},".rs"," file in ",[29,1181,1182],{},"src\u002Fbin\u002F"," becomes a separate binary target automatically. Run with ",[29,1185,1186],{},"cargo run --bin extra",[481,1188,1189,1061,1197,1200,1201,1050],{},[139,1190,1191,1194,1195],{},[29,1192,1193],{},"cargo run"," passes args after ",[29,1196,1112],{},[29,1198,1199],{},"cargo run -- --flag"," runs your binary with ",[29,1202,1203],{},"--flag",[481,1205,1206,1213,1214,1217,1218,1221],{},[139,1207,1208,1209,1212],{},"Multiple ",[29,1210,1211],{},"[[bin]]"," targets"," can share a ",[29,1215,1216],{},"src\u002Flib.rs"," for logic and have thin ",[29,1219,1220],{},"src\u002Fbin\u002F*"," shells.",[481,1223,1224,1061,1229,1232,1233,1235],{},[139,1225,1226,1228],{},[29,1227,83],{}," error codes",[29,1230,1231],{},"E0382"," etc. Search ",[29,1234,1064],{}," or online for detailed explanations.",[481,1237,1238,1061,1241,1244],{},[139,1239,1240],{},"Build scripts",[29,1242,1243],{},"build.rs"," runs before compilation; use for linking C libs, generating code at build time.",[481,1246,1247,1061,1253,296,1256,1259,1260,1050],{},[139,1248,1249,1252],{},[29,1250,1251],{},"CARGO_*"," env vars",[29,1254,1255],{},"CARGO_PKG_VERSION",[29,1257,1258],{},"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR",", etc., useful in build scripts and via ",[29,1261,1262],{},"env!",[14,1264,1266],{"id":1265},"reading-compiler-errors","Reading Compiler Errors",[78,1268,1269,1270,1273],{},"Rust errors are structured: the message, an ",[29,1271,1272],{},"-->"," pointing at the code, and often a help\u002Fnote. Multi-error cascades are common — fix the first error, then re-run; later ones often vanish.",[14,1275,1277],{"id":1276},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[78,1279,1280,1281,1284],{},"Why does ",[29,1282,1283],{},"cargo build"," succeed for one teammate and fail with a totally different error for another, on the exact same commit?",[19,1286,1287],{"language":644},[23,1288,1290],{"className":647,"code":1289,"language":644,"meta":27,"style":27},"[dependencies]\nsome_lib = \"1.2\"\n",[29,1291,1292,1296],{"__ignoreMap":27},[32,1293,1294],{"class":34,"line":35},[32,1295,706],{},[32,1297,1298],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,1299,1300],{},"some_lib = \"1.2\"\n",[1302,1303,1304,1308,1354,1360],"details",{},[1305,1306,1307],"summary",{},"Answer",[78,1309,1310,1311,1313,1314,1317,1318,1321,1322,1324,1325,1327,1328,1331,1332,1335,1336,1339,1340,1343,1344,1347,1348,1350,1351,1353],{},"The most common cause: one teammate has a ",[29,1312,971],{}," committed and checked out (or previously generated) that pins ",[29,1315,1316],{},"some_lib"," to, say, ",[29,1319,1320],{},"1.2.3",", while the other teammate either deleted their ",[29,1323,971],{},", is building a fresh checkout without one, or ran ",[29,1326,992],{}," locally — resolving ",[29,1329,1330],{},"\"1.2\""," (which means ",[29,1333,1334],{},"^1.2",", i.e., ",[29,1337,1338],{},">=1.2.0, \u003C2.0.0",") to a newer version like ",[29,1341,1342],{},"1.5.0"," that was published after the first teammate last locked their dependencies. Cargo.toml's version requirement is a ",[1115,1345,1346],{},"range",", not a pin — the actual, exact version used for any given build is determined by ",[29,1349,971],{},", and if that file is missing, out of date, or excluded from version control, two people (or two CI runs, or a local build vs. a Docker build) can silently resolve to different concrete versions of ",[29,1352,1316],{},", one of which may have introduced a breaking change or bug despite being \"semver compatible\" in theory.",[78,1355,1356,1357,1359],{},"This is precisely why the chapter's guidance is to always commit ",[29,1358,971],{}," for binaries (and, per current official guidance, for libraries too): it's the only thing that guarantees everyone — teammates, CI, and production builds — resolves the exact same dependency graph.",[78,1361,1362,1061,1365,1367,1368,1370,1371,1373,1374,1377],{},[139,1363,1364],{},"The lesson",[29,1366,640],{}," version requirements describe an acceptable ",[1115,1369,1346],{},"; only ",[29,1372,971],{}," pins the ",[1115,1375,1376],{},"exact"," versions actually used — an uncommitted or stale lock file means \"works on my machine\" can be literally true and still not mean what you think it means.",[14,1379,1380],{"id":1305},"Summary",[78,1382,1383],{},"You can scaffold, build, run, format, lint, and document a project. Next: the type system starts with variables and mutability.",[1385,1386,1387],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {c